#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124351 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124542 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/id #uuid "e9539818-ad55-5bb3-8c5d-5b85303f9e6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5521" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d82125089d15dada1be4f8d6669b5e125da921019b3a9d27376353dcf59a090.png)\n\nSuppose $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\rightarrow W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in V$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are shown above. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124352 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124543 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/id #uuid "8a371b65-8c57-5d10-88aa-2d4928fb028c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5522" :question/problem "![](images/8c/8caf13cdbf21ddfb1a121ede6ec0c21da155065905547bbd86b0e52cd57141da.png)\n\nConsider the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ (shown above) and a basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\nThe matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^3$ relative to these bases, and the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2,$ are also given. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}},$ the coordinates of $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}.$ So, let\n\n![](images/a5/a5b6f5f41dffd99a885bb872eac6f1e6a24bd604b360256194a0bf16b32ef381.png)\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -18\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/86/862742d57ad0ae4b56d6f345d825313bebf0d712f9c59ea1ed8b55d0a2eea22e.png)\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124415 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124603 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "01b46867-ba6d-5085-9543-b77ded581194" :question/math-academy-id "e-8604" :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf{T} : V \\rightarrow W$ is a linear map and $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\}$ and $\\mathcal{C} = \\{ \\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. Find the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1)=-3\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2,\\quad$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)=\\mathbf{c}_2-2\\mathbf{c}_1\\quad$ and $\\quad\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)=\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})={c}_{2}-2{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3})={c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/21/215cd69925ccfeab3ccb20874b7cdc2d837b99f33d8112f95fa5d2b646a27d40.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124416 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "3d6b0aec-c282-581e-ae4a-560654d80e3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8605" :question/problem "Consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3\\}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ given by\n![](images/7c/7c123e6f7d842a8e86e4c99826d25df070982514960752a25481a9f3f046cc1b.png)\n\nFind the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$ relative to these bases if \n![](images/9a/9a469219c661453d7891935b2ef0a32bff972bcf903d641ca7e31b7bec26369a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2),$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_i)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n![](images/9d/9d774b5bd79f14bc31e88a649fcb2a682d94ae3dd8acde5e25f52369c136e11e.png)\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -29 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/77/778f179c4681bcdcc5a64bcd128d946a272fa869289d2c2e542df75ad05850b6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124603 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3d3be8-279d-59f3-a2d8-12ca9d0cce23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269657} {:answer/id #uuid "89a50b23-711d-5633-b7dd-e7d9b60ebde7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270458} {:answer/id #uuid "aa59da11-d54d-5e37-89f9-271bc5567df8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270790} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7c4701-6312-5d0c-a55b-0246651198d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270920} {:answer/id #uuid "e9dc7fca-dda0-5add-b000-33287d932997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9dc7fca-dda0-5add-b000-33287d932997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271319} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b17c3e1-b262-584f-807c-5bfa08c55066" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9be338a6-16e6-59dc-a3ba-10e11d16158d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140430" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a507e0d-3567-5d61-bbe2-9d89591f6ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364991} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6167bb-8811-5823-8e3c-9c0a0fd96728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 12 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364992} {:answer/id #uuid "535b4647-2e3c-57e3-87ae-e2d55ffa67b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 & 12 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364993} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8e09ea-3cbb-5e01-b44d-76870dd03f37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364994} {:answer/id #uuid "a4772a99-ebf0-5414-abdd-91369dd717ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 & 12 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4772a99-ebf0-5414-abdd-91369dd717ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 & 12 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364995} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5d301bc-7c63-52f8-894b-ba3047b17af6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be3ad120-e4fe-5aa9-a7fc-db9ee09d2e87" :question/math-academy-id "q-140435" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{3})=[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 & 6 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 & -3 & 27\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 & -3 & 27\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -12 & -9 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -7 & -4 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 & 12 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088d91a0-3eaf-51f2-8ffe-b7c678ccdbc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388690} {:answer/id #uuid "a023134e-086b-501d-b434-5e8d31a4adbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388691} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0e6d22-1976-5811-872d-d23e457baf1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388692} {:answer/id #uuid "ad10460a-fb61-5b63-8b5e-2777f724a5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388693} {:answer/id #uuid "37fb40f0-005c-5d6e-98d1-6dd223500ce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab0e6d22-1976-5811-872d-d23e457baf1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388692} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d8dbb4a-8123-5815-85e7-0b6642b71201" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c5b8550-93bd-5bca-bdbb-d5d6c011cb4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140441" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124542 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4e4b448-5736-53e3-a65a-463590988a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}30 \\\\ 22\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364998} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a3bdc8-9672-51fc-883b-0d1165d6af56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364999} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b2ef62-f1a4-5edd-97b9-5821585d7733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365000} {:answer/id #uuid "66a67d29-d078-5904-993e-ee24b5ac6af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365001} {:answer/id #uuid "7498ad91-2492-509c-9756-44ed9464fbef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}36 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4a3bdc8-9672-51fc-883b-0d1165d6af56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364999} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbdc33cf-ea80-5d37-9fa6-790e78f0361d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a63da4eb-826f-555e-976d-87fcd38cb839" :question/math-academy-id "q-140443" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124542 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d47586c1-ff78-5ba9-89e3-901a684b6222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592