W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124603 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2acfdaf4-ddeb-5960-af3f-bf07ebb37aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324310} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb7950a-f63e-57c8-bd49-5541eedbdfed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324320} {:answer/id #uuid "8dde9e5d-1faf-54d1-b2ee-cb15e7135d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325175} {:answer/id #uuid "abbd0a26-3d78-52df-9ca6-4f1cb2764ac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325430} {:answer/id #uuid "daf7775c-80b3-5739-b811-ad0fba12860e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 &